{"cid": "UgzsVe1EAXc8bFxLauN4AaABAg", "text": "Why do Americans always add a quantifier to an absolute? 5:48 \"fits very perfectly,\" if it's perfect then it can't be more or less! Adding the qualifier downgrades the word's meaning, you guys have already ruined \"unique\" as continued use of \"very\" before it means we no longer have a word that means \"one of a kind\"", "time": "7 months ago (edited)", "author": "@cannissolis", "channel": "UCSFHzi6B5aO2gFrfD16x-Mg", "votes": "3", "replies": "", "photo": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_nU_pozvVljoUNqn0flQfJJT1YYqyylDYxrFwmfqlg=s88-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj", "heart": false, "reply": false, "time_parsed": 1748467739.713024}
